llowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14262417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### Description\n\nI have a [batch, vocab] logits matrix and a [batch] array of prng keys. I'd like to draw [batch] categorical samples, each governed by its own prng key.\nWithout explicit mesh, vmap works.\n\nWith explicit mesh, the only way I've figured out to make this work is to replicate the logits and prng keys. Replicating the logits is not a great workaround because it requires a lot of memory.\n\nRepro\n```python\nimport os\n\nos.environ[\"JAX_PLATFORMS\"] = \"cpu\"\nos.environ[\"XLA_FLAGS\"] = \"--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=4\"\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpy as np\nfrom jax.sharding import AxisType, Mesh, NamedSharding, PartitionSpec as P\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    devices = np.array(jax.devices()[:4]).reshape(2, 2)\n    mesh = Mesh(\n        devices, (\"data\", \"model\"), axis_types=(AxisType.Explicit, AxisType.Explicit)\n    )\n\n    # Sharded PRNG keys and logits — one per data shard                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n    keys = jax.random.split(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), 2)\n    keys = jax.device_put(keys, NamedSharding(mesh, P(\"data\")))\n    logits = jax.device_put(jnp.ones((2, 10)), NamedSharding(mesh, P(\"data\")))\n\n    print(f\"keys:   {jax.typeof(keys)}\")\n    print(f\"logits: {jax.typeof(logits)}\")\n\n    # BUG: vmap(categorical) with sharded keys fails.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \n    print(\"\\n--- vmap(categorical) with sharded keys: FAILS ---\")\n    try:\n\n        @jax.jit\n        def sample(keys: jax.Array, logits: jax.Array) -> jax.Array:\n            return jax.vmap(jax.random.categorical)(keys, logits)\n\n        print(f\"  result: {jax.typeof(sample(keys, logits))}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"  {type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n\n    # WORKAROUND: replicate inputs before vmap.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n    print(\"\\n--- workaround: replicate before vmap: WORKS ---\")\n    try:\n        repl = NamedSharding(mesh, P())\n\n        @jax.jit\n        def sample_repl(keys: jax.Array, logits: jax.Array) -> jax.Array:\n            return jax.vmap(jax.random.categorical)(\n                jax.reshard(keys, repl), jax.reshard(logits, repl)\n            )\n\n        print(f\"  result: {jax.typeof(sample_repl(keys, logits))}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"  {type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nRepro output\n```\nkeys:   uint32[2@data,2]\nlogits: float32[2@data,10]\n\n--- vmap(categorical) with sharded keys: FAILS ---\n  ValueError: Resource axis: data of PartitionSpec('data', None) is not found in mesh: ().\n\n--- workaround: replicate before vmap: WORKS ---\n  result: int32[2]\n```\n\nA little agent analysis of the root cause:\n```\nWhen PRNG keys are sharded on an explicit mesh and passed to                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \njax.random.categorical inside vmap, the PRNG primitive fails because                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \nthe abstract mesh context is empty inside vmap, but the key's sharding                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \nspec still references outer mesh axis names.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \nJAX source has a TODO acknowledging this (batching.py _batch_inner):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n  \"TODO(yashkatariya): Instead of `add_explicit_mesh_axis_names`, we should                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n   create a new mesh by removing the axis_data.explicit_mesh_axis from it.\"\n```\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n```\njax:    0.9.0.1\njaxlib: 0.9.0.1\nnumpy:  2.3.3\npython: 3.12.3 (main, Mar  3 2026, 12:15:18) [GCC 13.3.0]\ndevice info: cpu-1, 1 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nJAX_PLATFORMS=cpu\n```\n\n(but bug also reproduces on Jax 0.9.2)","closed_at":"2026-04-07T19:48:36Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/44061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copybara-service","id":56741989,"login":"copybara-service[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NTY3NDE5ODk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/36562/comments","created_at":"2026-04-07T16:38:39Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/36562/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/36562","id":4219189258,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1104782284,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTA0NzgyMjg0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/36562